@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.1865 = private unnamed_addr constant [13 x i8] c"raise-literal", align 1
@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.1866 = private unnamed_addr constant [521 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `raise` statements that raise a literal value.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`raise` must be followed by an exception instance or an exception class,\0Aand exceptions must be instances of `BaseException` or a subclass thereof.\0ARaising a literal will raise a `TypeError` at runtime.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Araise \22foo\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Araise Exception(\22foo\22)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `raise` statement](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/simple_stmts.html#the-raise-statement)\0A", align 1
