@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.1896 = private unnamed_addr constant [791 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for assignments with multiple or non-name targets in stub files.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIn general, stub files should be thought of as \22data files\22 for a type\0Achecker, and are not intended to be executed. As such, it's useful to\0Aenforce that only a subset of Python syntax is allowed in a stub file, to\0Aensure that everything in the stub is unambiguous for the type checker.\0A\0AThe need to perform multi-assignment, or assignment to a non-name target,\0Alikely indicates a misunderstanding of how stub files are intended to be\0Aused.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```pyi\0Afrom typing import TypeAlias\0A\0Aa = b = int\0A\0Aclass Klass: ...\0A\0AKlass.X: TypeAlias = int\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```pyi\0Afrom typing import TypeAlias\0A\0Aa: TypeAlias = int\0Ab: TypeAlias = int\0A\0Aclass Klass:\0A    X: TypeAlias = int\0A```\0A", align 1
@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.1897 = private unnamed_addr constant [70 x i8] c"Stubs should not contain assignments to attributes or multiple targets", align 1
