@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2086 = private unnamed_addr constant [12 x i8] c"blanket-noqa", align 1
@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2087 = private unnamed_addr constant [880 x i8] c"## What it does\0ACheck for `noqa` annotations that suppress all diagnostics, as opposed to\0Atargeting specific diagnostics.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ASuppressing all diagnostics can hide issues in the code.\0A\0ABlanket `noqa` annotations are also more difficult to interpret and\0Amaintain, as the annotation does not clarify which diagnostics are intended\0Ato be suppressed.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom .base import *  # noqa\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom .base import *  # noqa: F403\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule will attempt to fix blanket `noqa` annotations that appear to\0Abe unintentional. For example, given `# noqa F401`, the rule will suggest\0Ainserting a colon, as in `# noqa: F401`.\0A\0AWhile modifying `noqa` comments is generally safe, doing so may introduce\0Aadditional diagnostics.\0A\0A## References\0A- [Ruff documentation](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/configuration/#error-suppression)\0A", align 1
