@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2174 = private unnamed_addr constant [26 x i8] c"useless-object-inheritance", align 1
@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2175 = private unnamed_addr constant [392 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for classes that inherit from `object`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ASince Python 3, all classes inherit from `object` by default, so `object` can\0Abe omitted from the list of base classes.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Aclass Foo(object): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Aclass Foo: ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 3115 \E2\80\93 Metaclasses in Python 3000](https://peps.python.org/pep-3115/)\0A", align 1
