@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2205 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ ptr, [8 x i8], ptr, [8 x i8] }> <{ ptr @anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2203, [8 x i8] c"G\00\00\00\00\00\00\00", ptr @anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2204, [8 x i8] c"G\00\00\00\00\00\00\00" }>, align 8
@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2206 = private unnamed_addr constant [26 x i8] c"class-with-mixed-type-vars", align 1
@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2207 = private unnamed_addr constant [1236 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for classes that have [PEP 695] [type parameter lists]\0Awhile also inheriting from `typing.Generic` or `typing_extensions.Generic`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ASuch classes cause errors at runtime:\0A\0A```python\0Afrom typing import Generic, TypeVar\0A\0AU = TypeVar(\22U\22)\0A\0A# TypeError: Cannot inherit from Generic[...] multiple times.\0Aclass C[T](Generic[U]): ...\0A```\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Afrom typing import Generic, ParamSpec, TypeVar, TypeVarTuple\0A\0AU = TypeVar(\22U\22)\0AP = ParamSpec(\22P\22)\0ATs = TypeVarTuple(\22Ts\22)\0A\0A\0Aclass C[T](Generic[U, P, *Ts]): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Aclass C[T, U, **P, *Ts]: ...\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AAs the fix changes runtime behaviour, it is always marked as unsafe.\0AAdditionally, comments within the fix range will not be preserved.\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: User-defined generic types](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#user-defined-generic-types)\0A- [Python documentation: type parameter lists](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/compound_stmts.html#type-params)\0A- [PEP 695 - Type Parameter Syntax](https://peps.python.org/pep-0695/)\0A\0A[PEP 695]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0695/\0A[type parameter lists]: https://docs.python.org/3/reference/compound_stmts.html#type-params\0A", align 1
